That is a deeper test, because the victim of torture is now innocent from the start. At first the comparison is balanced: $\text{one innocent girl tortured}
\qquad \text{vs.} \qquad
\text{one innocent child saved}.$ The utilitarian initially refuses this one-for-one case. The reason is not mysterious: the child being tortured is as innocent as the child being saved. So innocence is isolated as a distinct variable. We are no longer trading on the guilt of the kidnapper.

